The time zone from tzset

Valkey writes its log's times itself and takes the time zone from the
C library's timezone, which tzset sets, on Linux and Solaris, and
elsewhere from the second argument of gettimeofday, which POSIX leaves
unspecified and mlibc does not fill: its log read "-558737 Jan 1970".
Radix's C library sets timezone as Linux's does, so Radix takes it too.

diff --git a/src/util.c b/src/util.c
index 5c7cd5a..f884667 100644
--- a/src/util.c
+++ b/src/util.c
@@ -1254,7 +1254,7 @@ sds getAbsolutePath(char *filename) {
  * i.e timezone variables are linux specific.
  */
 long getTimeZone(void) {
-#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__sun)
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__sun) || defined(__radix__)
     return timezone;
 #else
     struct timezone tz;
